      "title": "‘Perfect weapon’: diabetic woman found guilty of murdering her 94-year-old parents with insulin",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/20/diabetic-woman-found-guilty-murdering-94-year-old-parents-with-insulin-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Jury convicts Raelene Polymiadis after four-month trial in South Australian supreme court</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A jury has convicted a diabetic woman of murdering both her elderly parents with insulin after a marathon criminal trial.</p><p>Raelene Polymiadis, 66, will face two mandatory life sentences after jurors on Friday delivered unanimous verdicts after a four-month South Australian supreme court trial.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/20/diabetic-woman-found-guilty-murdering-94-year-old-parents-with-insulin-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-20T04:15:16"
    },
    {
      "title": "Religion should be removed from terrorism definition under Australian law as it gives ‘false credibility’, watchdog says",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2026/nov/20/religion-should-removed-from-terrorism-definition-australian-law-gives-false-credibility-watchdog-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Independent National Security Legislation Monitor says reference to religion has ‘contributed to discrimination and violence against religious minorities’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Religion should be removed from Australia’s terrorism definition and making bomb threats should not result in life imprisonment, the country’s national security laws watchdog has said.</p><p>The highly anticipated report from the Independent National Security Legislation Monitor (INSLM), released Thursday, reviewed how terrorism has been defined in Australia over the past 25 years after a suite of laws were introduced following the September 11 attacks in the United States.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/law/2026/nov/20/religion-should-removed-from-terrorism-definition-australian-law-gives-false-credibility-watchdog-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-20T00:19:57"
    },
    {
      "title": "US warned supplying nuclear-powered submarines to Australia would diminish its own fleet for ‘many years’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/20/aukus-defence-us-warned-supplying-nuclear-powered-submarines-to-australia-would-diminish-its-own-fleet-for-many-years",
      "description": "<p>Congressional Budget Office also questions whether Australian-flagged vessels could be compelled into a conflict with China under Aukus deal</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Providing nuclear-powered submarines to Australia would diminish the US navy’s own fleet for “many years”, a new report for the US Congress has cautioned, questioning whether Australian-flagged vessels could be compelled into service in a conflict with China.</p><p>The US navy’s <a href=\"https://media.defense.gov/2026/May/11/2003928909/-1/-1/1/NAVY%20SHIPBUILDING%20PLAN%20MAY%202026.PDF\">latest shipbuilding plan</a> does not countenance the Aukus agreement in its forecasts at all, noting only in a footnote that the transfer of any Virginia-class submarine to Australia “has not been factored into the plan”, the report says.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/20/aukus-defence-us-warned-supplying-nuclear-powered-submarines-to-australia-would-diminish-its-own-fleet-for-many-years\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-20T00:16:29"
    },
